18 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt (Diagram showing effects of various stress conditions on three plant species: Cai xin, lettuce, and spinach. Part A displays plant images under different conditions like phosphate, potassium, nitrate levels, temperature, light intensity, photoperiod, and light quality. Part B shows a color-coded heatmap scoring these conditions. Part C features a bar graph indicating the number of differentially expressed genes, divided into up-regulated and down-regulated categories, across the stress conditions for each plant species.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 57 0 R /Alt (A multi-panel image showing a heatmap, a level chart, and a network diagram related to plant species and metabolic processes. Panel A displays a heatmap with colored boxes representing regulation of processes across various species and stresses. Panel B presents a heatmap of normalized differential expression indices. Panel C illustrates network diagrams across different levels, depicting connections between processes, marked with varied colors to denote distinct functions.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 58 0 R /Alt (Complex infographic depicting gene expression analysis across three plant species: Cai Xin, Lettuce, and Spinach. Part A shows a heatmap with color codes for upregulated \(red\) and downregulated \(blue\) genes under various conditions like nitrogen and phosphate deficiency. Part B is a bar chart illustrating conserved differentially expressed genes \(DEGs\) across stresses, with categories such as salt, cold, and light. Part C and D are bar charts showing conserved orthogroups interacting with specific stress sets, highlighted in red for upregulation and blue for downregulation. Labels, axes, and color legends provide detailed context.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 59 0 R /Alt (Panel A is an infographic detailing a process for identifying conserved TF-target edges in three species using GENIE3. Panel B is a bar chart comparing the number of conserved edges across species. Panel C is a heatmap displaying enrichment scores and p-values for cross-species conservation. Panel D presents complex network diagrams with nodes representing enzymes and proteins, categorized by function. A legend explains node shapes and colors.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 60 0 R /Alt (Diagram displaying two main sections. A\) Circular networks illustrate biological responses to potassium, nitrogen, and phosphate deficiencies, temperature, and photoperiod. B\) A hierarchical network map outlines gene interactions, split into Levels 1, 2, and 3, with emphasis on transcriptional repressors, photosynthesis, and lipid metabolism, ending at a terminal node. Each node is color-coded for different biological processes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 46 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 61 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a bar graph illustrating average expression profiles with varied colored bars. Panel B features a complex gene network diagram with interconnected labeled nodes. Panel C is a heatmap with genes and varying colors indicating responses to different conditions like drought and heat. Panel D presents a Venn diagram with overlapping circles showing gene intersections between two species, accompanied by a list detailing gene families and types.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 48 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
